// Text, the breaks between it, and the characters in it that would otherwise
// be markup.

--- paragraphs ---
First paragraph.

Second paragraph.
│ <p>First paragraph.</p>
│ <p>Second paragraph.</p>

--- linebreak ---
One line \
and the next.
│ <p>One line<br>and the next.</p>

--- escaping-in-text ---
// The three characters that would otherwise start markup are escaped; a quote
// is left alone, because in text it reads as itself.
a \< b \& c \> d "e"
│ <p>a &lt; b &amp; c &gt; d “e”</p>

--- horizontal-space ---
Left#h(1em)right.
│ <p>Left<span style="display:inline-block;width:1em"></span>right.</p>

--- horizontal-space-points ---
Left#h(6pt)right.
│ <p>Left<span style="display:inline-block;width:6pt"></span>right.</p>

--- horizontal-space-mixed ---
Left#h(6pt + 1em)right.
│ <p>Left<span style="display:inline-block;width:calc(6pt + 1em)"></span>right.</p>

--- text-with-explicit-spacing ---
#text("  spaced  out  ")
│ <p>spaced  out</p>

--- nonbreaking-and-unicode ---
naïve — résumé … ✓
│ <p>naïve — résumé … ✓</p>
